WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.610 --> 00:08.738
Read forwards or backwards, my name is Minami Minamida.

3
00:08.822 --> 00:10.240
Autism Spectrum Disorder?

4
00:10.323 --> 00:12.033
Her background isn't bad, right?

5
00:12.116 --> 00:13.868
If she isn't at the level to stand in court,

6
00:13.952 --> 00:15.745
will you reconsider her employment?

7
00:15.829 --> 00:16.996
You did it! See?

8
00:17.080 --> 00:19.374
The victim died while being transported.

9
00:19.457 --> 00:20.959
Maybe being a lawyer

10
00:21.042 --> 00:23.169
was impossible for me with autism after all.

11
00:23.253 --> 00:24.838
Unless the prosecution

12
00:24.921 --> 00:27.132
can medically prove a causal relationship

13
00:27.215 --> 00:30.009
between the defendant's strike and the resulting death,

14
00:30.093 --> 00:33.179
the defendant cannot be held criminally responsible!

15
00:35.765 --> 00:40.478
The time has come for the two of you to take a step toward your new life.

16
00:41.020 --> 00:42.939
Please rise

17
00:43.022 --> 00:45.942
and give a big round of applause for the bride and groom.

18
00:47.235 --> 00:49.654
The bride and groom will now make their exit.

19
02:15.406 --> 02:18.368
HIROKAWA &amp; HOWARD LPC NEW ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

20
02:18.451 --> 02:20.787
Don't push yourself. Use the stairs.

21
02:20.870 --> 02:23.706
-Good morning, Ms. Asahi. -Morning.

22
02:23.790 --> 02:25.708
I'm waiting for someone right now.

23
02:25.792 --> 02:26.876
Someone?

24
02:27.502 --> 02:28.670
Talking about whales.

25
02:29.254 --> 02:31.089
Isn't it fine when it's just the two of us?

26
02:32.215 --> 02:33.091
What?

27
02:33.174 --> 02:35.802
That's why I'm waiting here for Mr. Funai.

28
02:36.511 --> 02:38.763
What's going on with you two?

29
02:38.846 --> 02:40.515
ATTORNEY TAKUMA HIMI

30
02:40.598 --> 02:42.308
Wouldn't Funai already be here?

31
02:43.434 --> 02:45.395
Good morning, Mr. Himi.

32
02:45.478 --> 02:47.438
If Mr. Funai is here, I'll go now.

33
02:48.731 --> 02:51.317
Good morning, Ms. Minamida.

34
02:51.401 --> 02:53.277
Good morning, Managing Partner.

35
02:53.361 --> 02:54.487
HIROKAWA - TSUCHIMURA

36
02:54.570 --> 02:57.198
How's work? Take your time getting used to it.

37
02:57.865 --> 02:59.659
Yes, I'll take my time.

38
02:59.742 --> 03:02.745
Is the Managing Partner greeting Ms. Minamida herself?

39
03:02.829 --> 03:04.205
No, it's a coincidence.

40
03:04.288 --> 03:05.748
If you ever need anything,

41
03:05.832 --> 03:07.291
just tell me.

42
03:07.375 --> 03:08.501
Anything?

43
03:10.670 --> 03:12.463
-Have a good one. -You too.

44
03:20.513 --> 03:23.433
So Ms. Minamida was raised by a single father.

45
03:25.810 --> 03:27.770
Managing Partner, they've arrived.

46
03:30.440 --> 03:32.900
We've been expecting you, Chairman.

47
03:33.693 --> 03:35.153
-See? -It's been a while.

48
03:35.236 --> 03:36.904
Thank you for coming.

49
03:36.988 --> 03:39.407
I'm pretty sure that man is…

50
03:40.450 --> 03:42.452
How much do you think that wedding cost?

51
03:43.244 --> 03:45.955
I trusted those hotel guys to provide top-tier service,

52
03:46.039 --> 03:47.415
and it cost 30 million yen!

53
03:47.498 --> 03:48.499
PARTNER ATTORNEY MIYAJI

54
03:48.583 --> 03:50.293
Here is the breakdown.

55
03:50.376 --> 03:51.919
I'll send it via email later as well.

56
03:52.003 --> 03:54.088
I paid 30 million

57
03:54.172 --> 03:57.633
just to be completely humiliated in front of a huge crowd of guests.

58
03:57.717 --> 03:59.635
I completely understand how you feel.

59
04:00.345 --> 04:03.514
So, how much can we get from the hotel?

60
04:05.516 --> 04:08.394
That man from earlier is the Chairman of Kurasawa Food Systems.

61
04:09.520 --> 04:12.023
Apparently, his daughter had her wedding

62
04:12.106 --> 04:13.858
with the heir of Mikoshiba Land Development,

63
04:14.734 --> 04:18.279
but her wedding dress slipped down in the middle of the ceremony,

64
04:18.363 --> 04:21.491
leaving her fully exposed in front of a huge crowd.

65
04:21.991 --> 04:22.992
So her underwear…

66
04:26.704 --> 04:27.622
Wow…

67
04:28.247 --> 04:29.123
Wow…

68
04:33.586 --> 04:35.546
-Welcome back, sir. -Welcome back.

69
04:35.630 --> 04:36.964
I'm at my wits' end.

70
04:37.924 --> 04:40.468
That man from earlier, he's from Kurasawa Food Systems--

71
04:40.551 --> 04:41.552
The Chairman, right?

72
04:41.636 --> 04:43.888
Mr. Himi was gossiping that his daughter's

73
04:43.971 --> 04:45.348
wedding dress slipped down.

74
04:45.431 --> 04:47.975
What? I-- I just happened to overhear it!

75
04:48.059 --> 04:51.771
But Kurasawa Food Systems isn't one of our corporate clients, are they?

76
04:51.854 --> 04:55.608
Up until now, they had a corporate retainer with MMK Law Firm.

77
04:55.691 --> 04:57.860
But MMK turned this case down,

78
04:57.944 --> 04:59.904
-so he came to us, their rival. -And?

79
05:01.864 --> 05:04.075
The hotel offered a full refund of the wedding costs

80
05:04.158 --> 05:06.994
plus hotel vouchers worth 5 million yen,

81
05:07.078 --> 05:08.746
but he said that isn't enough.

82
05:08.830 --> 05:10.748
I think that's not bad compensation.

83
05:10.832 --> 05:12.083
-Right? -Yes.

84
05:12.166 --> 05:14.210
But he demands at least 100 million.

85
05:14.293 --> 05:15.378
100 million?

86
05:15.461 --> 05:18.756
The secretary emailed the details. I'll forward them,

87
05:18.840 --> 05:20.216
-so take a look. -What?

88
05:20.299 --> 05:21.634
Did you actually accept the case?

89
05:21.717 --> 05:22.885
Yeah.

90
05:23.428 --> 05:26.431
The Managing Partner got fired up

91
05:26.514 --> 05:29.016
the moment she heard MMK.

92
05:29.100 --> 05:30.435
What did you say just now?

93
05:30.518 --> 05:34.063
I said this place is just like MMK.

94
05:34.772 --> 05:36.440
You run away when a case

95
05:36.524 --> 05:38.693
is too big to handle. Am I wrong?

96
05:41.070 --> 05:43.990
The amount you want is 100 million, correct?

97
05:44.073 --> 05:46.200
Understood. We'll take the case.

98
05:46.284 --> 05:47.285
Really?

99
05:47.785 --> 05:48.995
You'll do it!

100
05:49.579 --> 05:51.622
You really are different from MMK!

101
05:51.706 --> 05:52.623
Yes.

102
05:52.748 --> 05:56.085
Hirokawa &amp; Howard LPC is on your side.

103
05:56.169 --> 05:59.755
HIROKAWA &amp; HOWARD LPC IS ON YOUR SIDE

104
06:03.301 --> 06:06.596
MANAGING PARTNER NAGISA HIROKAWA

105
06:09.640 --> 06:10.558
So,

106
06:10.641 --> 06:13.561
let's all put our heads together to figure out how to bill

107
06:13.644 --> 06:15.104
the hotel for 100 million.

108
06:16.355 --> 06:19.275
We can claim the roughly 30 million yen

109
06:19.358 --> 06:21.110
already paid for the wedding as damages,

110
06:21.194 --> 06:22.862
but we need to get the remaining

111
06:22.945 --> 06:24.780
70 million out of emotional distress damages.

112
06:24.864 --> 06:28.117
In this case, 5 million is the best we could do, right?

113
06:28.201 --> 06:30.620
It'd be different if we had grounds to really increase

114
06:30.703 --> 06:31.996
the emotional distress damages.

115
06:32.079 --> 06:34.916
Apparently, the bride herself says the dress was weird.

116
06:34.999 --> 06:37.126
The dress was a rental, right?

117
06:37.210 --> 06:39.170
If there was a problem with the dress,

118
06:39.253 --> 06:41.672
we can hold the hotel responsible since they arranged it.

119
06:42.340 --> 06:44.467
Assuming there was gross negligence,

120
06:44.550 --> 06:46.677
the hotel will likely try to hide it.

121
06:46.761 --> 06:49.722
DESIRED CLAIM AMOUNT FROM HOTEL: MINIMUM 100 MILLION

122
06:50.890 --> 06:53.100
Let's go undercover for this one.

123
06:53.184 --> 06:54.518
Undercover?

124
06:55.353 --> 06:56.437
I say that,

125
06:56.520 --> 07:00.191
but you'll just go as customers and try on dresses.

126
07:00.274 --> 07:01.943
Mr. Himi and Ms. Asahi, can you manage?

127
07:02.026 --> 07:03.152
Yes.

128
07:03.236 --> 07:05.112
We are the engaged couple?

129
07:05.196 --> 07:06.989
Yeah. And Ms. Minamida,

130
07:07.073 --> 07:10.034
you and Funai go talk to the bride and groom.

131
07:10.117 --> 07:11.202
Yes, understood.

132
07:14.205 --> 07:15.540
Could I go to the hotel

133
07:16.415 --> 07:18.626
with Mr. Funai instead of Mr. Himi?

134
07:27.510 --> 07:28.886
KURASAWA

135
07:28.970 --> 07:30.596
Why did Ms. Asahi

136
07:30.680 --> 07:32.640
hate the idea of you being her fiancé?

137
07:32.723 --> 07:34.183
She didn't say she hated it.

138
07:34.267 --> 07:36.102
She just said she preferred Funai.

139
07:36.185 --> 07:37.937
I also wanted to go with Mr. Funai.

140
07:38.896 --> 07:39.855
Is that so?

141
07:40.356 --> 07:42.066
Well, I'm sorry about that.

142
07:43.734 --> 07:44.860
You are Ms. Hirono, right?

143
07:45.444 --> 07:47.446
We are here at your father's request.

144
07:47.530 --> 07:49.865
I'm Himi from Hirokawa &amp; Howard LPC.

145
07:49.949 --> 07:51.200
It is a pleasure to meet you.

146
07:51.284 --> 07:52.660
Hello.

147
07:53.327 --> 07:54.579
Ms. Minamida…

148
07:54.662 --> 07:56.539
Please introduce yourself as well.

149
08:01.419 --> 08:03.462
It's a pleasure. I'm Minamida.

150
08:03.546 --> 08:05.214
ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

151
08:06.966 --> 08:07.925
Minami Minamida?

152
08:08.009 --> 08:08.968
Yes!

153
08:09.051 --> 08:11.721
Read forwards or backwards, it's Minami Minamida.

154
08:11.804 --> 08:14.932
Kayak, deed, rotator, civic, racecar, Minami Minamida.

155
08:15.016 --> 08:15.850
What?

156
08:15.933 --> 08:18.019
I apologize. She just joined the firm recently.

157
08:19.270 --> 08:20.730
-I see. -Yes.

158
08:22.732 --> 08:24.191
Please have a seat.

159
08:24.275 --> 08:25.318
Thank you.

160
08:26.944 --> 08:28.863
Have you seen your husband since then?

161
08:29.572 --> 08:30.740
I haven't seen him.

162
08:31.907 --> 08:36.120
Actually, he told me he wants to call off the marriage altogether.

163
08:37.371 --> 08:39.081
Is the dress incident the reason?

164
08:39.832 --> 08:42.251
I have a tattoo on my back.

165
08:42.335 --> 08:43.377
A tattoo?

166
08:48.424 --> 08:49.925
It's a magnolia, isn't it?

167
08:51.302 --> 08:53.721
It seems he couldn't accept the fact

168
08:53.804 --> 08:56.015
that the guests saw my tattoo.

169
08:57.183 --> 08:59.602
When did you notice something was wrong with the dress?

170
08:59.685 --> 09:01.270
The morning of the wedding.

171
09:01.854 --> 09:04.357
It fit perfectly at the fitting,

172
09:04.440 --> 09:05.900
but it was loose that day.

173
09:05.983 --> 09:07.318
You must have lost weight.

174
09:07.401 --> 09:09.945
I told the hotel staff, too,

175
09:10.029 --> 09:11.947
but they said it was because I lost weight.

176
09:12.573 --> 09:14.992
So, I had them take the dress in.

177
09:16.035 --> 09:19.163
Excuse me for asking, but why did you rent your dress?

178
09:19.747 --> 09:21.123
I just assumed

179
09:21.207 --> 09:23.793
the Kurasawa family would naturally go for a custom-made dress.

180
09:25.252 --> 09:28.547
I didn't invite anyone I know to the wedding.

181
09:29.131 --> 09:29.965
Not one person?

182
09:30.049 --> 09:31.550
My father organized the wedding,

183
09:31.634 --> 09:33.844
so the guests were all just his acquaintances.

184
09:34.720 --> 09:37.431
That's why I didn't particularly care.

185
09:37.515 --> 09:39.100
I see.

186
09:40.267 --> 09:42.478
Ms. Minamida, is there anything you'd like to ask?

187
09:43.062 --> 09:43.896
Yes, there is.

188
09:45.606 --> 09:48.401
Ms. Hirono, do you love your husband?

189
09:48.484 --> 09:49.735
What?

190
09:49.819 --> 09:51.028
Why ask that out of nowhere?

191
09:51.112 --> 09:53.989
Even if you couldn't show it to your friends,

192
09:54.073 --> 09:58.786
wouldn't you want your husband to see you in a dress you cared about?

193
10:01.288 --> 10:03.249
Congratulations on your Coming of Age, Ririi!

194
10:03.332 --> 10:04.625
The kimono looks great on you.

195
10:04.709 --> 10:05.751
Where's Minami?

196
10:05.835 --> 10:06.752
MINAMI'S DAD MAKOTO

197
10:06.836 --> 10:08.045
Well…

198
10:11.048 --> 10:13.259
You're not wearing a kimono?

199
10:13.342 --> 10:15.761
It felt like a kelp roll, and it was too uncomfortable.

200
10:15.845 --> 10:18.723
You put so much thought into that outfit.

201
10:18.806 --> 10:21.350
Don't you want to show it off at least a little?

202
10:22.059 --> 10:24.061
That's what my father said.

203
10:25.187 --> 10:27.314
I apologize for her sudden, rude question.

204
10:33.612 --> 10:35.239
-Something wrong with the dress? -Yes.

205
10:35.823 --> 10:38.409
Ms. Hirono said she felt it. Did you know about it?

206
10:38.492 --> 10:40.286
No, I didn't know.

207
10:40.369 --> 10:41.370
I see.

208
10:42.288 --> 10:45.374
By the way, why do you want to call off the marriage?

209
10:45.458 --> 10:46.500
Do I have to answer?

210
10:46.584 --> 10:47.793
No.

211
10:47.877 --> 10:50.755
Ms. Hirono said the tattoo on her back was the reason.

212
10:50.838 --> 10:51.797
Hey…

213
10:53.507 --> 10:55.718
Yes. That's right.

214
10:56.260 --> 10:58.888
I knew about the tattoo before the wedding.

215
10:59.513 --> 11:01.766
She got it on a whim when she was young,

216
11:02.266 --> 11:04.310
and I told her I didn't mind.

217
11:04.393 --> 11:05.227
Then why…

218
11:05.311 --> 11:08.481
Other people knowing about it is a different story.

219
11:08.564 --> 11:10.649
My family and business partners

220
11:10.733 --> 11:14.069
won't necessarily be so accepting of it.

221
11:14.737 --> 11:17.364
Luckily, we haven't filed our marriage papers yet.

222
11:25.539 --> 11:26.457
Are we done?

223
11:26.540 --> 11:29.168
I have my next meeting soon.

224
11:31.212 --> 11:32.755
Can I ask a question, too?

225
11:33.339 --> 11:34.882
-Go ahead. -Are you sure?

226
11:34.965 --> 11:35.925
Yes.

227
11:37.384 --> 11:38.802
Do you love your wif--

228
11:41.263 --> 11:44.850
Excuse us. We'll be leaving now. Ms. Minamida, let's go.

229
11:44.934 --> 11:47.478
Let's go. Come on.

230
11:47.561 --> 11:49.522
MIKOSHIBA LAND DEVELOPMENT

231
11:50.564 --> 11:54.318
Calling you "Mr. Funai" would be weird, right?

232
11:55.361 --> 11:56.570
What do you mean?

233
11:57.363 --> 11:59.073
How we call each other.

234
11:59.156 --> 12:01.867
We're supposed to be engaged, after all.

235
12:03.494 --> 12:04.912
That's true.

236
12:05.579 --> 12:08.624
Then, shall we call each other by our first names?

237
12:09.208 --> 12:10.626
Minato and Koharu.

238
12:14.088 --> 12:17.174
Wouldn't it sound more authentic if we dropped the honorifics?

239
12:17.758 --> 12:19.218
Then… Koharu.

240
12:22.096 --> 12:23.264
Yes.

241
12:25.891 --> 12:28.852
Also, I thought up a backstory for us.

242
12:28.936 --> 12:29.812
Okay.

243
12:29.895 --> 12:31.772
We've been dating for six months.

244
12:31.855 --> 12:33.440
We met at the gym.

245
12:33.524 --> 12:36.235
We started talking after seeing each other a lot.

246
12:36.318 --> 12:38.237
That sounds pretty realistic.

247
12:38.320 --> 12:40.281
The reason we're rushing the marriage

248
12:40.364 --> 12:43.951
is because a slightly impatient little angel has come to us.

249
12:44.034 --> 12:44.868
A little angel?

250
12:44.952 --> 12:48.581
Minato… said we should do it before my belly starts showing.

251
12:49.873 --> 12:52.376
I told him we didn't need a wedding, but…

252
12:52.459 --> 12:55.337
No way. I want to cherish this milestone with you, Koharu.

253
12:56.255 --> 12:57.214
Okay.

254
13:01.385 --> 13:03.012
ATTORNEY TAKUMA HIMI

255
13:04.972 --> 13:06.015
Go ahead.

256
13:10.185 --> 13:11.020
Yes.

257
13:11.103 --> 13:14.231
We're done interviewing the bride and groom, so I wanted to report back.

258
13:14.315 --> 13:16.483
She said the dress felt off, too.

259
13:16.567 --> 13:19.403
I see. Thank you.

260
13:19.486 --> 13:22.364
But rich families are such a pain.

261
13:22.448 --> 13:24.908
The bride is a puppet, and the groom

262
13:24.992 --> 13:28.662
-isn't committed. In this day and age… -Hirokawa &amp; Howard LPC is on your side.

263
13:28.746 --> 13:31.540
he's calling off the marriage just over a tattoo.

264
13:31.624 --> 13:34.376
Mr. Himi, if this story is going to take a while…

265
13:34.460 --> 13:36.629
could you just send it in a message?

266
13:36.712 --> 13:38.130
Thank you.

267
13:42.509 --> 13:43.469
Shall we go?

268
13:43.552 --> 13:44.511
Yes.

269
13:47.848 --> 13:50.309
Where did we leave off in our story?

270
13:51.018 --> 13:53.395
I was saying I want to cherish our milestone.

271
13:53.479 --> 13:54.438
Right.

272
13:54.521 --> 13:56.482
And so, since we're doing this…

273
13:58.859 --> 14:00.527
It's my phone this time. Sorry.

274
14:01.487 --> 14:02.696
ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

275
14:03.280 --> 14:04.114
Yes, hello.

276
14:04.198 --> 14:06.158
Did you know that no human

277
14:06.241 --> 14:08.619
has ever seen a blue whale give birth?

278
14:08.702 --> 14:09.745
What?

279
14:09.828 --> 14:12.081
I thought I should share the whale talk

280
14:12.164 --> 14:14.333
I had planned to tell you today, Mr. Funai.

281
14:14.416 --> 14:16.794
We haven't done that yet today, have we?

282
14:17.628 --> 14:19.964
It makes you wonder why, considering a blue whale

283
14:20.047 --> 14:22.091
the size of an airplane gives birth to a calf

284
14:22.174 --> 14:23.467
as heavy as a hippo, but…

285
14:23.550 --> 14:26.053
Hey… what are you talking about?

286
14:27.179 --> 14:28.514
Ms. Asahi?

287
14:29.098 --> 14:31.058
About a blue whale giving birth.

288
14:32.059 --> 14:34.603
We're working, so aren't you bothering him?

289
14:37.231 --> 14:38.315
It's fine.

290
14:38.899 --> 14:41.610
Ms. Minamida, I'm busy now, so I'll call you later.

291
14:42.194 --> 14:43.112
Okay.

292
14:45.030 --> 14:46.240
Is she always like this?

293
14:46.824 --> 14:48.867
Well… sometimes.

294
14:55.374 --> 14:56.417
Yes, hello.

295
14:57.418 --> 15:00.421
Did you know that fin whales are migratory animals?

296
15:00.504 --> 15:01.588
What?

297
15:01.672 --> 15:04.675
And yet, a pod of 400 whales living in the Gulf of California

298
15:04.758 --> 15:07.344
stays in the exact same spot and refuses to move.

299
15:08.554 --> 15:10.973
Yes. Right now…

300
15:12.558 --> 15:13.600
Hello?

301
15:14.810 --> 15:16.311
Ms. Minamida?

302
15:18.188 --> 15:20.232
Whales feed deep in the ocean,

303
15:20.315 --> 15:21.775
then surface to defecate.

304
15:22.359 --> 15:23.235
You startled me…

305
15:23.318 --> 15:25.529
The reason blue whale feces is red

306
15:25.612 --> 15:27.573
is because their main diet, krill, is red.

307
15:27.656 --> 15:29.158
I see.

308
15:29.241 --> 15:32.494
How is that "sometimes"? She is practically stalking you.

309
15:33.203 --> 15:34.580
I don't mind.

310
15:34.663 --> 15:36.331
I learn a lot,

311
15:36.415 --> 15:38.959
and besides, I want to be there to listen to her.

312
15:43.338 --> 15:44.423
Can you…

313
15:44.965 --> 15:46.675
keep that up for the rest of your life?

314
15:46.759 --> 15:47.593
What?

315
15:48.469 --> 15:50.345
If you don't have that resolve,

316
15:50.429 --> 15:52.347
you should draw a line, Mr. Funai.

317
15:53.432 --> 15:56.477
Wouldn't that be what is best for her?

318
16:04.026 --> 16:05.360
Are you okay?

319
16:05.444 --> 16:07.321
What do you mean?

320
16:20.417 --> 16:21.460
Excuse me.

321
16:25.339 --> 16:27.716
It's definitely the boiled egg…

322
16:55.369 --> 16:57.287
Ms. Minamida, why are you here?

323
16:58.038 --> 16:59.623
I cannot say why I am here.

324
16:59.706 --> 17:02.167
Especially not to you, Mr. Funai. Absolutely not.

325
17:04.920 --> 17:06.213
Where's Ms. Asahi?

326
17:12.136 --> 17:13.887
Ms. Asahi? I'm here.

327
17:14.847 --> 17:16.181
Over here! Give it to me!

328
17:21.937 --> 17:23.397
Hey, what is this?

329
17:23.480 --> 17:25.524
My suit pants were in my locker, right?

330
17:25.607 --> 17:26.608
They were.

331
17:27.109 --> 17:29.319
Then why did you bring this?

332
17:29.820 --> 17:31.738
It looked like the easiest thing to put on.

333
17:33.407 --> 17:35.951
Give me a break…

334
17:41.123 --> 17:42.583
ASAHI

335
17:47.171 --> 17:48.589
Should I get you another outfit?

336
18:00.267 --> 18:01.560
Ms. Asahi?

337
18:02.644 --> 18:04.730
I'm done for.

338
18:06.190 --> 18:09.359
I yield this marriage to you.

339
18:11.153 --> 18:14.364
Take good care of… Minato.

340
18:22.748 --> 18:25.417
Please. If any dresses catch your eye,

341
18:25.500 --> 18:27.085
feel free to take it off the rack.

342
18:28.837 --> 18:29.963
Yes.

343
18:30.839 --> 18:32.674
We've been dating for six months.

344
18:32.758 --> 18:34.509
We met at the gym.

345
18:34.593 --> 18:36.595
We're rushing the wedding because Ms. Asahi…

346
18:36.678 --> 18:40.098
I mean, an impatient little angel in my belly.

347
18:41.558 --> 18:42.559
Is that so?

348
18:44.603 --> 18:48.565
This dress would look great on you, Minami!

349
18:49.316 --> 18:51.193
It's very lovely.

350
18:51.276 --> 18:53.278
Would you like to try it on?

351
18:53.362 --> 18:56.448
Excuse me, about this dress… I'm very sorry.

352
18:57.366 --> 18:58.909
Why is this out here?

353
19:08.752 --> 19:10.712
Is there a problem with that dress?

354
19:10.796 --> 19:11.755
No, honestly,

355
19:11.838 --> 19:15.509
that type of dress is out of fashion, so we're swapping it out.

356
19:15.592 --> 19:17.928
You also have to be careful wearing it.

357
19:18.011 --> 19:19.263
You're right.

358
19:19.346 --> 19:21.014
Minami is petite.

359
19:21.098 --> 19:23.517
It'd be a disaster if it slipped down.

360
19:23.600 --> 19:24.893
Does that ever happen?

361
19:24.977 --> 19:26.561
That would never happen.

362
19:26.645 --> 19:28.480
We ensure the fitting is perfect.

363
19:29.481 --> 19:31.817
We have a design that would look great on you,

364
19:31.900 --> 19:33.527
so I'll go prepare it.

365
19:33.610 --> 19:35.362
Right this way to the fitting room.

366
19:44.621 --> 19:47.749
Sir! That area is for employees only.

367
19:48.709 --> 19:50.127
-Is that so? -Yes.

368
19:50.210 --> 19:51.211
I'm sorry.

369
19:57.926 --> 20:00.470
Hello, Ms. Asahi, are you okay now?

370
20:01.763 --> 20:04.182
So she's carrying a white dress.

371
20:04.891 --> 20:06.226
I'll try to find her.

372
20:39.968 --> 20:41.428
I just can't do it…!

373
20:42.763 --> 20:45.098
KOHARU ASAHI: I'M SORRY! I COULDN'T DO IT!

374
20:47.559 --> 20:50.562
Sir, the bride has finished changing.

375
20:51.480 --> 20:52.564
Okay.

376
21:21.676 --> 21:23.136
How does it feel?

377
21:24.304 --> 21:26.139
I feel like a cabbage roll.

378
21:26.223 --> 21:27.391
It's so uncomfortable.

379
21:29.226 --> 21:32.437
My, my. The groom is completely captivated.

380
21:34.272 --> 21:35.607
Are you captivated?

381
21:39.736 --> 21:40.862
CREATIVE RICE BALLS

382
21:40.946 --> 21:42.823
-I'm home. -Welcome back. You're late.

383
21:43.573 --> 21:45.617
The Minami Minamida set is ready.

384
21:45.700 --> 21:48.078
I'm doing the dishes, so take your lunchbox out.

385
21:48.161 --> 21:49.329
Wash your hands first.

386
21:56.169 --> 21:58.255
I said take your lunchbox out.

387
22:05.637 --> 22:06.721
What's this?

388
22:14.229 --> 22:16.857
"Special Maternity Wedding Plan"?

389
22:16.940 --> 22:18.108
What?

390
22:19.484 --> 22:22.404
What? No… Hey, calm down.

391
22:22.487 --> 22:24.239
No. Minami, getting married?

392
22:24.322 --> 22:25.991
Maternity? No way!

393
22:26.074 --> 22:27.868
No! That's impossible!

394
22:27.951 --> 22:29.202
There's no way.

395
22:34.833 --> 22:36.459
Mr. Minamida, is Minami home?

396
22:36.543 --> 22:37.794
Welcome, Ririi.

397
22:37.878 --> 22:39.421
Minami is washing her hands.

398
22:41.590 --> 22:42.924
You're hungry, right?

399
22:43.008 --> 22:45.760
I'll make you a prototype brown sugar ohagi.

400
22:45.844 --> 22:46.970
Brown sugar ohagi?

401
22:47.053 --> 22:48.763
Yes! Now, sit down.

402
22:51.474 --> 22:52.475
So…

403
22:52.559 --> 22:55.353
What kind of things do you talk about with Minami lately?

404
22:56.354 --> 22:57.689
Do you girls talk about boys?

405
22:58.899 --> 23:00.108
Not really.

406
23:00.192 --> 23:01.818
Right. Not really.

407
23:03.320 --> 23:06.156
Hey, did you see this? Minami sent it to me.

408
23:11.161 --> 23:13.288
Minami!

409
23:14.164 --> 23:15.415
Minami to the Minamida!

410
23:15.498 --> 23:16.750
Ririi to the Madoka!

411
23:21.671 --> 23:23.798
-By the way, Dad… -I don't want to hear it!

412
23:23.882 --> 23:25.800
I'm not listening!

413
23:26.760 --> 23:28.303
I'm absolutely not listening!

414
23:30.430 --> 23:31.681
My lunchbox…

415
23:32.349 --> 23:34.309
-Enjoy your meal. -Thank you.

416
23:37.354 --> 23:38.480
Minato?

417
23:39.231 --> 23:40.232
Yes.

418
23:42.484 --> 23:43.318
Minato.

419
23:43.401 --> 23:45.070
What is it?

420
23:45.153 --> 23:47.614
You are "Minato," Mr. Funai.

421
23:47.697 --> 23:49.574
Minato and Minami are only one letter apart.

422
23:50.367 --> 23:52.077
Come to think of it, you're right.

423
23:52.994 --> 23:54.579
Your name is a palindrome,

424
23:54.663 --> 23:57.707
but in kanji,

425
23:57.791 --> 24:00.168
it's also symmetrical left to right.

426
24:00.919 --> 24:04.631
My dad named me after a manga character, Minami Asakura.

427
24:06.591 --> 24:08.718
Your name, Minato,

428
24:08.802 --> 24:11.346
means a harbor where ships set sail into the ocean.

429
24:11.429 --> 24:12.264
Yes.

430
24:13.181 --> 24:15.642
A harbor is a place where you can go to meet whales.

431
24:15.725 --> 24:18.728
I feel like I might meet a whale when I'm with you.

432
24:19.896 --> 24:20.855
I see.

433
24:22.899 --> 24:25.110
I like the name Minato.

434
24:28.113 --> 24:29.364
Thank you.

435
24:31.366 --> 24:36.162
Do you have anything to talk to me about besides whales?

436
24:37.998 --> 24:38.832
I don't.

437
24:41.626 --> 24:42.669
I see.

438
24:43.503 --> 24:44.546
You don't.

439
24:54.055 --> 24:55.807
Hello. Are you heading to lunch?

440
24:56.808 --> 24:58.518
It's you two. Why are you here?

441
24:58.601 --> 25:00.061
We were lying in wait.

442
25:00.145 --> 25:02.397
We're actually from a law firm.

443
25:02.480 --> 25:03.606
PARALEGAL MINATO FUNAI

444
25:04.274 --> 25:07.319
At the wedding on October 11th, a dress slipped off, didn't it?

445
25:07.402 --> 25:09.321
We have some questions about that.

446
25:09.404 --> 25:11.740
Where did you take this dress?

447
25:12.782 --> 25:14.034
I don't know anything…

448
25:14.117 --> 25:15.994
If you're worried

449
25:16.077 --> 25:18.788
about any repercussions, please be rest assured.

450
25:19.539 --> 25:22.459
Hirokawa &amp; Howard LPC is on your side!

451
25:23.626 --> 25:24.586
On your side.

452
25:30.884 --> 25:32.927
COURTHOUSE

453
25:34.554 --> 25:35.597
FIRST HEARING: WITNESS EXAM

454
25:35.680 --> 25:37.140
Witness, I understand

455
25:37.223 --> 25:40.268
you helped fit Ms. Hirono's dress on the day of the wedding.

456
25:40.852 --> 25:44.397
Do you remember what Ms. Hirono said when she put the dress on?

457
25:45.398 --> 25:46.232
Yes.

458
25:47.609 --> 25:49.778
I feel like it's a little loose.

459
25:51.571 --> 25:53.323
You must have lost weight.

460
25:53.907 --> 25:57.118
It's common for brides to diet and lose weight

461
25:57.202 --> 25:58.912
before the day of the wedding.

462
25:58.995 --> 26:03.458
Besides, this dressmaker is highly skilled and has a good reputation,

463
26:03.541 --> 26:05.251
so I didn't think the dress was the cause.

464
26:06.211 --> 26:07.962
Do you still think so?

465
26:17.555 --> 26:19.307
Well? Do you still think so now?

466
26:22.977 --> 26:23.978
No.

467
26:26.689 --> 26:28.316
Why is that?

468
26:29.901 --> 26:31.986
After the wedding ended,

469
26:32.070 --> 26:34.781
I learned it had been swapped with a different dress.

470
26:38.284 --> 26:40.328
Apparently, on the morning of the wedding,

471
26:40.412 --> 26:44.541
a new staff member tore the dress we had prepared.

472
26:44.624 --> 26:46.501
What are you crying for!

473
26:46.584 --> 26:48.461
They didn't have time to fix it,

474
26:48.545 --> 26:52.632
so they swapped it with a slightly larger one of the same design.

475
26:52.715 --> 26:56.928
In other words, the staff hid that fact from Ms. Hirono, didn't they?

476
26:57.637 --> 27:02.016
The chief told me I'd be fired if I leaked it outside.

477
27:03.977 --> 27:07.564
I'm so sorry for keeping this to myself.

478
27:12.986 --> 27:13.987
Nothing further.

479
27:22.745 --> 27:25.373
Plaintiff, have you been suffering this whole time?

480
27:26.207 --> 27:27.041
What?

481
27:27.876 --> 27:28.710
Yes.

482
27:28.793 --> 27:32.881
Do you have a social media account under the handle "Magnolia"?

483
27:32.964 --> 27:33.798
What?

484
27:33.882 --> 27:34.757
Please answer.

485
27:36.801 --> 27:37.635
Yes.

486
27:38.720 --> 27:39.554
Your Honor.

487
27:39.637 --> 27:42.056
I would like to submit new evidence, if I may.

488
27:42.140 --> 27:43.433
What is this about?

489
27:44.851 --> 27:49.439
I found posts from an account believed to be the plaintiff's,

490
27:49.522 --> 27:52.358
-and I just confirmed it's hers. -Objection.

491
27:53.860 --> 27:56.988
I do not believe the plaintiff's personal social media posts

492
27:57.071 --> 27:58.531
are relevant to this dispute.

493
27:58.615 --> 27:59.616
Objection overruled.

494
28:03.203 --> 28:07.832
These posts were made from this account on or after October 11th,

495
28:07.916 --> 28:09.834
the day of the wedding.

496
28:12.462 --> 28:15.340
"He told me he wants to call off the marriage altogether."

497
28:16.090 --> 28:18.218
"I find myself feeling relieved."

498
28:19.511 --> 28:21.971
"I won't have to go through with a fake marriage."

499
28:22.639 --> 28:25.183
"I should be grateful the wedding was ruined."

500
28:28.728 --> 28:32.482
Earlier, you admitted you had been "suffering this whole time."

501
28:32.565 --> 28:35.944
Yet you're suing the hotel for a massive 100 million yen

502
28:36.027 --> 28:38.363
in emotional distress damages.

503
28:38.446 --> 28:40.281
How do you really feel?

504
28:42.242 --> 28:43.701
What exactly was painful?

505
28:54.420 --> 28:56.172
If you don't tell us,

506
28:56.798 --> 28:59.384
we can't help you either.

507
29:05.390 --> 29:07.183
I originally met him

508
29:07.267 --> 29:09.769
through an arranged marriage set up by our parents.

509
29:11.104 --> 29:13.022
He took a liking to me,

510
29:14.315 --> 29:16.526
and things just kept moving forward…

511
29:17.861 --> 29:20.071
Especially since my father was so eager.

512
29:20.154 --> 29:22.699
He'd enter into the Mikoshiba family, after all.

513
29:23.283 --> 29:24.742
There was that,

514
29:25.410 --> 29:29.205
but I think what my father was really happy about was the bonus.

515
29:29.289 --> 29:30.540
The bonus?

516
29:30.623 --> 29:32.834
During our families' first meeting,

517
29:32.917 --> 29:36.838
his grandfather said he would give me a 500-tsubo plot of land

518
29:37.463 --> 29:39.883
in Yokohama as a wedding gift.

519
29:41.009 --> 29:43.094
My father had even made plans

520
29:43.177 --> 29:45.096
for how to use that land.

521
29:47.015 --> 29:48.057
But honestly,

522
29:48.725 --> 29:52.228
part of me wondered if this was really the right choice.

523
29:52.312 --> 29:54.480
So that's why you posted that on social media.

524
29:55.189 --> 29:58.318
I know it was a stupid thing to do.

525
30:02.989 --> 30:04.699
HOTEL CLAIM: MINIMUM 100 MILLION

526
30:04.782 --> 30:06.200
DAMAGES EMOTIONAL DISTRESS

527
30:06.284 --> 30:08.453
MINIMUM 100 MILLION

528
30:22.675 --> 30:25.011
Ms. Hirono, it is a good thing there was a bonus!

529
30:25.094 --> 30:25.970
What?

530
30:26.846 --> 30:28.848
Damages are divided into two categories,

531
30:28.932 --> 30:31.684
general damages and special damages, did you know that?

532
30:33.019 --> 30:34.896
Are you testing me?

533
30:36.814 --> 30:40.777
General damages are damages that ordinarily arise.

534
30:40.860 --> 30:44.739
Special damages are damages that arise from extraordinary circumstances.

535
30:44.822 --> 30:47.825
In this case, the wedding costs fall under general damages,

536
30:47.909 --> 30:49.702
but they only amount to about 30 million,

537
30:49.786 --> 30:51.871
making it difficult to claim 100 million.

538
30:52.455 --> 30:54.332
However, in reality, Ms. Hirono had a bonus,

539
30:54.415 --> 30:57.794
that is, the special circumstance of the land gift.

540
30:57.877 --> 31:02.799
This makes the marriage conditional on the promised gift of the land.

541
31:02.882 --> 31:05.051
If the dress hadn't slipped off at the wedding,

542
31:05.134 --> 31:07.845
the groom wouldn't have called off the marriage,

543
31:07.929 --> 31:10.348
and the land would have been gifted as promised.

544
31:10.431 --> 31:13.518
If we claim the value of the land

545
31:13.601 --> 31:15.561
Ms. Hirono lost as special damages,

546
31:15.645 --> 31:18.106
we can demand a much larger compensation payout.

547
31:18.189 --> 31:21.359
Best of all, we no longer need to fixate on emotional distress damages.

548
31:21.442 --> 31:24.862
Whatever the cause of your mental suffering was,

549
31:24.946 --> 31:27.156
it has nothing to do with special damages.

550
31:27.240 --> 31:29.867
By the way, do you know the land's estimated value?

551
31:30.451 --> 31:32.662
My dad said something like three billion yen.

552
31:35.498 --> 31:38.209
If we claim that three billion as damages,

553
31:38.292 --> 31:40.545
the other side will likely offer a settlement.

554
31:41.212 --> 31:44.007
Ten percent of three billion is 300 million.

555
31:44.090 --> 31:45.800
We can negotiate from there.

556
31:47.760 --> 31:52.640
First, we must confirm this strategy with your father.

557
31:53.433 --> 31:55.476
-Mr. Himi, will you come with me? -Yes.

558
31:55.560 --> 31:57.437
I'll try drafting the brief.

559
31:57.520 --> 31:58.980
Yeah. Excuse us.

560
32:00.982 --> 32:01.816
Thank you.

561
32:06.904 --> 32:08.698
It's okay. I'm sure it'll go well.

562
32:09.615 --> 32:11.034
What do you mean, "go well"?

563
32:14.537 --> 32:18.332
My dress slipped down and my wedding was ruined, right?

564
32:19.208 --> 32:21.919
What good would it do to demand money

565
32:22.003 --> 32:23.463
just because we're upset

566
32:23.546 --> 32:25.298
about not getting the land?

567
32:26.299 --> 32:29.010
-But the hotel was negligent-- -Did I--

568
32:29.093 --> 32:31.429
Did I ever say I wanted money?

569
32:32.555 --> 32:34.182
It's my case.

570
32:34.265 --> 32:35.767
It's my wedding.

571
32:36.350 --> 32:38.311
But nobody cares about me!

572
32:39.103 --> 32:41.647
Everyone only cares about my father.

573
32:43.941 --> 32:47.320
Is it difficult to tell your father how you feel?

574
32:49.697 --> 32:51.991
How am I supposed to talk to someone

575
32:52.075 --> 32:53.826
who won't even lend an ear?

576
32:55.453 --> 32:58.122
I've given up on everything,

577
32:58.623 --> 33:00.458
from college to jobs.

578
33:03.961 --> 33:05.296
It's fine.

579
33:05.379 --> 33:09.092
I can't leave my parents anyway.

580
33:14.347 --> 33:15.807
I'm going home.

581
33:30.321 --> 33:31.989
HOW LONG WILL I KEEP RUNNING AWAY?

582
33:43.334 --> 33:44.877
Minami, you're home.

583
33:45.920 --> 33:48.464
Dad, if you could get a lot of money

584
33:48.548 --> 33:50.716
from the person I marry, would you be happy?

585
33:50.800 --> 33:51.968
What?

586
33:52.760 --> 33:53.636
Why all of a sudden?

587
33:53.719 --> 33:54.887
-Would you be happy? -Hold on.

588
33:55.555 --> 33:56.472
Hold on.

589
33:58.015 --> 34:01.644
Before talking about money, you have something to tell me, right?

590
34:02.728 --> 34:05.565
I found someone who will listen to me talk about whales,

591
34:05.648 --> 34:07.567
so I don't need to tell you.

592
34:09.485 --> 34:10.528
I see.

593
34:11.487 --> 34:14.240
You found someone like that.

594
34:24.876 --> 34:25.877
Listen, Minami.

595
34:26.919 --> 34:28.421
More than money,

596
34:28.504 --> 34:29.964
I'm worried about

597
34:30.047 --> 34:32.341
whether you'll be able to make it on your own

598
34:32.925 --> 34:34.510
from now on.

599
34:35.511 --> 34:36.721
Okay.

600
34:37.305 --> 34:39.140
I don't know what kind of guy he is,

601
34:40.099 --> 34:42.143
but there's no guarantee

602
34:42.226 --> 34:44.520
he'll do things the same way I have.

603
34:46.397 --> 34:49.150
From now on, you need to be able to prepare

604
34:49.817 --> 34:51.944
the Minami Minamida set yourself.

605
34:52.028 --> 34:52.945
By myself?

606
34:53.529 --> 34:55.072
Leaving your parents

607
34:56.073 --> 34:58.409
and becoming independent, that is what it's all about.

608
34:59.911 --> 35:01.204
Independent adults

609
35:02.079 --> 35:04.624
prepare their own meals.

610
35:13.674 --> 35:15.301
Why are you crying, Dad?

611
35:15.384 --> 35:16.302
Be quiet.

612
35:16.385 --> 35:19.430
My head is a mess, so I don't know either!

613
35:22.058 --> 35:23.100
But Minami…

614
35:24.977 --> 35:26.062
congrats on your marriage.

615
35:28.356 --> 35:30.566
I'm getting married?

616
35:32.568 --> 35:33.486
What?

617
35:34.946 --> 35:35.863
You're not?

618
35:45.831 --> 35:47.792
300 million instead of 100 million.

619
35:47.875 --> 35:49.335
You really are different from MMK.

620
35:49.418 --> 35:51.003
We still have the witness exam.

621
35:51.087 --> 35:55.216
First, we must prove the hotel president knew about the land gift.

622
35:55.299 --> 35:56.133
It's fine.

623
35:56.842 --> 35:59.887
He was there at the families' meeting too. Right?

624
36:01.097 --> 36:01.931
Yeah.

625
36:02.431 --> 36:03.599
Then, right this way.

626
36:08.562 --> 36:09.689
Ms. Hirono.

627
36:14.443 --> 36:17.947
This is the very first salted rice ball I've ever made.

628
36:18.948 --> 36:20.157
Please have it, if you'd like.

629
36:28.541 --> 36:32.128
Ms. Hirono, have you ever prepared your own meals?

630
36:32.920 --> 36:34.630
I never had.

631
36:36.007 --> 36:37.008
Why do you ask that?

632
36:38.134 --> 36:40.261
My father told me that

633
36:40.344 --> 36:43.139
all independent adults prepare their own meals.

634
36:43.222 --> 36:45.850
I prepared my meal, so today,

635
36:45.933 --> 36:48.769
I became independent from my father.

636
36:49.937 --> 36:53.190
I hope you can become independent from your father, too.

637
36:58.738 --> 36:59.739
2ND HEARING: WITNESS EXAM

638
36:59.822 --> 37:01.657
A wedding gift, you say?

639
37:02.199 --> 37:03.701
The groom's grandfather

640
37:03.784 --> 37:07.496
said he would give the plaintiff a 500-tsubo plot of land in Yokohama,

641
37:07.580 --> 37:10.791
and I hear you praised him, saying, "How generous."

642
37:12.793 --> 37:14.962
I was merely stating a fact.

643
37:15.046 --> 37:16.005
So,

644
37:16.589 --> 37:20.676
you knew the groom's grandfather promised the plaintiff

645
37:20.760 --> 37:24.638
land worth billions as a wedding gift?

646
37:26.640 --> 37:27.641
Yes.

647
37:29.602 --> 37:30.478
Thank you.

648
37:34.231 --> 37:35.649
Your Honor.

649
37:35.733 --> 37:38.611
The plaintiff had a special circumstance where land would be gifted

650
37:38.694 --> 37:41.530
on the condition of marriage, and the defendant was aware of it.

651
37:41.614 --> 37:43.866
Therefore, the plaintiff claims

652
37:43.949 --> 37:48.120
3.3 billion yen in damages for the land she would've obtained.

653
37:49.872 --> 37:52.875
Please allow us to amend the claim and cause of action.

654
37:52.958 --> 37:55.002
I see no reason to deny it.

655
37:55.086 --> 37:57.296
Please submit the motion to amend.

656
37:57.380 --> 37:58.214
Yes.

657
38:00.925 --> 38:02.843
Is there anything else?

658
38:04.428 --> 38:05.388
Excuse me…

659
38:06.180 --> 38:07.515
What is it, plaintiff?

660
38:08.265 --> 38:10.351
I want to drop the lawsuit.

661
38:10.434 --> 38:11.394
What?

662
38:15.147 --> 38:17.316
I'm dropping the lawsuit!

663
38:34.834 --> 38:36.252
How do I stop it?

664
38:40.297 --> 38:43.426
How do I get the criminal charges dropped?

665
38:46.512 --> 38:48.681
"Criminal charges" are for criminal cases.

666
38:49.557 --> 38:53.144
In this case, you might want to ask how to drop the lawsuit.

667
38:54.770 --> 38:57.982
How do I… drop the lawsuit?

668
38:59.191 --> 39:02.027
There are two ways to drop a lawsuit.

669
39:02.111 --> 39:03.279
The easier one, please.

670
39:04.238 --> 39:05.614
If you turn to the judge

671
39:05.698 --> 39:07.575
and say, "I'm dropping the lawsuit,"

672
39:07.658 --> 39:08.951
it will be dropped.

673
39:10.995 --> 39:11.912
Is that it?

674
39:12.621 --> 39:14.165
Yes, that's it.

675
39:15.708 --> 39:17.001
That's easy.

676
39:18.335 --> 39:19.295
Yes.

677
39:19.378 --> 39:21.672
It's easier than making a salted rice ball.

678
39:25.342 --> 39:27.511
Why couldn't I do this sooner?

679
39:29.096 --> 39:30.222
Are you an idiot?

680
39:30.806 --> 39:32.683
They just admitted they knew about the land!

681
39:32.766 --> 39:35.603
The gallery will refrain from making unsolicited remarks.

682
39:37.104 --> 39:38.230
Plaintiff.

683
39:40.274 --> 39:42.109
If you drop the lawsuit,

684
39:42.193 --> 39:45.988
the claim will be treated as if it never existed. Are you sure?

685
39:46.071 --> 39:46.906
Yes.

686
39:48.157 --> 39:50.409
Defendant, do you consent?

687
39:50.993 --> 39:52.328
Yes, I consent.

688
39:54.580 --> 39:57.917
With the withdrawal of the lawsuit, this case is concluded.

689
39:58.501 --> 39:59.585
Court is adjourned.

690
40:16.435 --> 40:18.479
Do you have any idea what you just did?

691
40:19.355 --> 40:20.689
This is…

692
40:20.773 --> 40:22.775
my case,

693
40:22.858 --> 40:24.652
my wedding,

694
40:24.735 --> 40:26.195
and my life!

695
40:26.278 --> 40:27.988
Don't get smart with me!

696
40:33.994 --> 40:35.120
You don't know

697
40:35.204 --> 40:38.457
a single thing about my true feelings, Dad.

698
40:38.541 --> 40:40.000
There's no way you would.

699
40:40.960 --> 40:42.378
You haven't noticed a thing,

700
40:43.921 --> 40:45.756
even though we've been together

701
40:45.839 --> 40:47.716
for ten years.

702
41:03.649 --> 41:05.859
The magnolia flower

703
41:06.610 --> 41:07.987
on my back

704
41:08.779 --> 41:10.614
is to carve into my body

705
41:10.698 --> 41:12.741
my unwavering feelings for Hasumi.

706
41:19.832 --> 41:21.000
WEDDING PAYMENT DETAILS

707
41:21.083 --> 41:22.543
SENDER: HASUMI MIZUKI

708
41:22.626 --> 41:23.961
MAGNOLIA

709
41:24.044 --> 41:26.922
So that's why it was "Magnolia"…

710
41:27.506 --> 41:28.966
If I'm getting married,

711
41:29.049 --> 41:31.135
it's going to be with her.

712
41:31.802 --> 41:33.470
Because Hasumi

713
41:34.263 --> 41:36.015
is the one I love.

714
41:36.765 --> 41:37.891
Wow…

715
41:37.975 --> 41:39.184
Wow…

716
41:45.649 --> 41:46.775
Are you okay?

717
42:11.675 --> 42:12.968
Shinji Mikoshiba!

718
42:14.386 --> 42:15.596
What is it?

719
42:15.679 --> 42:17.348
The lawsuit was dropped, right?

720
42:18.098 --> 42:19.808
The lawsuit was dropped.

721
42:19.892 --> 42:21.727
But there's something bothering me.

722
42:23.854 --> 42:27.232
Do you love Hirono, Shinji?

723
42:30.194 --> 42:31.320
Why would you ask that?

724
42:32.363 --> 42:35.074
Because the lock screen on your smartphone

725
42:35.157 --> 42:37.326
is a photo of Hirono.

726
42:44.625 --> 42:45.793
Are we done?

727
42:45.876 --> 42:47.961
I have my next meeting soon.

728
42:49.963 --> 42:53.008
My friend told me you'd normally hate to even look

729
42:53.092 --> 42:56.887
at the person you're calling off a marriage with.

730
43:03.686 --> 43:04.937
I see!

731
43:05.020 --> 43:09.066
You realized Hirono liked someone else,

732
43:09.149 --> 43:11.485
so you called off the marriage for her sake.

733
43:12.528 --> 43:14.196
If so, it all makes sense.

734
43:18.659 --> 43:20.202
You're overthinking it.

735
43:26.083 --> 43:27.751
I'm overthinking it?

736
43:29.336 --> 43:31.255
People's feelings are complicated.

737
43:37.386 --> 43:38.512
Ms. Minamida.

738
43:39.430 --> 43:40.264
Minato.

739
43:40.347 --> 43:42.891
We haven't had our whale talk today yet, have we?

740
43:43.392 --> 43:45.227
Want to talk on the way back?

741
43:46.311 --> 43:47.146
Yes!

742
43:48.605 --> 43:51.817
But from now on, let's set a time to talk.

743
43:54.194 --> 43:55.154
Okay.

744
43:59.366 --> 44:01.493
Do you know about the humpback whale song?

745
44:01.577 --> 44:02.411
What?

746
44:02.494 --> 44:03.662
The humpback whale song is…

747
44:03.746 --> 44:07.207
I'm sorry we couldn't reach a settlement.

748
44:07.291 --> 44:08.876
It's more than enough.

749
44:08.959 --> 44:13.005
The Chairman highly evaluated our work.

750
44:13.839 --> 44:17.468
He says they're putting us on retainer from now on.

751
44:17.551 --> 44:20.137
I see. That's good to hear.

752
44:20.220 --> 44:23.891
But the idea of special damages was interesting.

753
44:23.974 --> 44:26.810
Ms. Minamida might become an unexpected asset for us.

754
44:27.394 --> 44:28.312
"Unexpected"?

755
44:29.062 --> 44:30.606
Didn't you hire her, Managing Partner?

756
44:30.689 --> 44:32.232
What?

757
44:32.316 --> 44:33.859
Of course, I did.

758
44:33.942 --> 44:36.153
I just meant more than I expected.

759
44:44.703 --> 44:49.708
Subtitle translation by: Hasan Hüseyin Öztürk

760
44:49.792 --> 44:50.667
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

761
44:50.751 --> 44:53.170
The brother who committed the assault is autistic.

762
44:54.338 --> 44:55.756
If you want answers,

763
44:55.839 --> 44:57.966
try digging into what he likes.

764
44:58.050 --> 44:59.635
Do I really have to do this?

765
44:59.718 --> 45:01.553
Ultraman Zero!

766
45:04.431 --> 45:07.184
Shut up! You're autistic too, aren't you?

767
45:08.268 --> 45:10.896
It seems there's someone else besides the defendant.

768
45:10.979 --> 45:12.814
I can't be of any help to the defendant.

769
45:12.898 --> 45:13.732
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
